"funil.leitura": "The darker band shows where 95% of municipalities of each size would fall according to the model; the lighter one, {p998}. Small municipalities vary more just because they are small: the top of a ranking of small municipalities is not, by itself, a pattern. The band comes from a model: it shows how much a municipality of that size usually varies.",
"funil.leg95": {"t": "95% band", "rotulo": 20},
"funil.leg998": {"t": "{p998} band", "rotulo": 20},
"funil.leg_dentro": {"t": "inside the band", "rotulo": 20},
"funil.leg_fora": {"t": "outside the {p998} band", "rotulo": 30},
"funil.leg_acima": {"t": "outside, above: change in Lula's share", "rotulo": 48},
"funil.leg_abaixo": {"t": "outside, below: Flávio's", "rotulo": 32},
"funil.dica_fatia": {"t": "Change in Lula's share", "rotulo": 30},
"funil.dica_abstencao": {"t": "Change in abstention", "rotulo": 30},
"funil.fonte": "Source: TSE, results by municipality; band from the Spiegelhalter model (2005a, 2005b); our calculations.",
"funil.como.tit": "How the funnel band works",
"funil.como.1": "Center: the change for all {mun} municipalities combined. Band: center ± z × √(chance error² + τ²), where the chance error depends only on the number of registered voters and τ² is a variation common to all municipalities, estimated from the data (z = {z95} for 95% and {z998} for {p998}).",
"funil.como.2": "Under the model, about 5% would fall outside the 95% band by chance; {fora} did, and from {pmin} to {pmax} in each size group. τ² is estimated with all municipalities, without trimming the tails; with 10% trimmed from each tail, as in the original method, the band came out too narrow for medium and large municipalities and {fw} fell outside. A variation common to all municipalities is a simplification when the variation depends on size (Xia et al., 2022).",
"funil.como.2_abst": "For abstention, {acima} of the {fora95} municipalities outside the 95% band are above it: the distribution has a long upper tail, and the symmetric band does not fit it. A point above the band means that abstention rose more than in most municipalities of that size, not how rare that is.",
"funil.como.3": "Limit: the band comes from a model and serves as a screen, to decide what to look at closely (Spiegelhalter et al., 2012); a municipality outside it is not, on its own, proof of anything.",

