// --- Chapter 9: the guided exploration (T33; HIPOTESES.md, section 8, round 1) ---
"c9.pergunta": "What else do the data show?",
"c9.curto": {"t": "What else the data show", "rotulo": 30},
"c9.resposta": "There were ten questions, in two rounds, asked after seeing the results. The clearest answers: Lula overtook Flávio in {fl} municipalities, and Flávio overtook Lula in {lf}; the other candidates' votes did not tilt the same way: in the polling-station calculation, the net of Augusto Cury's votes tilted to Lula, and the net of Ronaldo Caiado's to Flávio; and, in the first round, just over half of voters aged 70 or over turned out ({p70}).",
"c9.rotulo.cab": "Exploratory, not recorded before the calculations. ",
"c9.rotulo.texto": "The questions in this chapter were asked after seeing the results of chapters 1 to 8, in two rounds, and chosen with the author. Each one was recorded before running, with the test and what would count as a finding, and all of them are shown here, with or without a finding.",
"c9.rotulo.res": "Result: in the first round of questions, a finding in {n} of the 4 questions with an estimate and {s} without a firm answer (the other one is a count); in the second, four counts and one estimate, {r2}. Among several questions asked after seeing the data, a finding may turn up by chance. ",
"c9.rotulo.curto": "Exploratory, not recorded before the calculations.",
"c9.cand.70": {"t": "Augusto Cury (Avante)", "fixo": true},
"c9.cand.70.curto": {"t": "A. Cury", "fixo": true},
"c9.cand.14": {"t": "Renan Santos (Missão)", "fixo": true},
"c9.cand.14.curto": {"t": "R. Santos", "fixo": true},
"c9.cand.55": {"t": "Ronaldo Caiado (PSD)", "fixo": true},
"c9.cand.55.curto": {"t": "R. Caiado", "fixo": true},
"c9.cand.resto": {"t": "The other seven, combined", "rotulo": 30},
"c9.cand.resto.curto": {"t": "Other 7 cand.", "rotulo": 16},
"c9.e1.p": "Where did the votes of each of the other candidates go?",
"c9.e1.r": "They did not go the same way: most of Augusto Cury's votes went to Lula ({l70}); most of Ronaldo Caiado's ({f55}) and of the seven smaller candidates' combined ({fresto}) went to Flávio; Renan Santos's had no clear direction (figure {fig}).",
"c9.e2.p": "In how many municipalities did one overtake the other?",
"c9.e2.r": "Lula overtook Flávio in {fl} municipalities, home to {el} registered voters; Flávio overtook Lula in {lf}, home to {ellf} registered voters. Lula's share of the two-candidate vote rose in {sub} of the {tot} municipalities, and Flávio's in {caiu}. It is a count, with no model (figure {fig}).",
"c9.e3.p": "Did abstention change differently in the states with a runoff for governor?",
"c9.e3.r": "No clear difference. Abstention changed, on average, by {a1} in those 6 states and by {a2} in the other 21, a difference that may be chance alone and that disappears when states in the same region are compared.",
"c9.e4.p": "Did turnout rise more where Lula was stronger or where Flávio was stronger?",
"c9.e4.r": "Slightly more where Lula was stronger: comparing polling stations in the same city, abstention fell {iq} more in those in the quarter with the most Lula votes in the first round than in those in the quarter with the most Flávio votes, a small difference (figure {fig}).",
"c9.e5.p": "Did each candidate gain more where he was weaker, also when comparing polling stations in the same city?",
"c9.e5.r": "No firm answer. Without correction, yes, as across municipalities (chapter 1); with the chance correction recorded before the calculation, the opposite, but that correction tends to overcorrect when the voters are the same in both rounds (“See details”, question 5).",
"c9.e1.sec": "1. The votes of each of the other candidates",
"c9.e2.sec": "2. Municipalities where one overtook the other",
"c9.e3.sec": "3. Abstention in the states with a runoff for governor",
"c9.e4.sec": "4. Turnout and each candidate's strength, within the city",
"c9.e5.sec": "5. Where each candidate was weaker, within the city",
"c9.link.c1": "Exploratory, not recorded before the calculations: the same question, comparing polling stations in the same city, with no firm answer.",
"c9.link.c3": "Exploratory, not recorded before the calculations: where the votes of each of the other candidates went, separately.",
"c9.link.c4": "Exploratory, not recorded before the calculations: abstention in the states with a runoff for governor, turnout where each candidate was stronger, and who voted and who stayed away, by age.",
"c9.link.ir": {"t": "See in chapter 9", "rotulo": 24},
"c9.e1.lado.l": "most to Lula",
