// ---------- Step by step (metodo.js) ----------
"met.passo.intro": "From the TSE file to the number on screen, in the order the calculations run. Each step is a Python script that reads the output of the previous step, checks what it read and writes a new file; run in order, they rebuild everything from the raw files. The page does no new calculation: it reads the last file and rounds each number once, when it is displayed.",
"met.passo.n": "Step {n}",
"met.passo.cadeia_aria": "Scripts and files of step {n}",
"met.passo.baixar": "To download: {arquivos}.",
"met.passo.repo": "The scripts, the datasets they write and the record of the hypotheses are in the {repo}, with step-by-step instructions to rebuild everything from the sources. The datasets the page uses are also in {baixar}.",
"met.passo.1.tit": "Download and check the first round",
"met.passo.1.txt": "The first-round presidential result, municipality by municipality, from the TSE's official files. The sum of the {mun} municipalities equals the sum of the states, the national file and the official result.",
"met.passo.2.tit": "Download and check the runoff",
"met.passo.2.txt": "The same for the runoff, with 100% of voting machines counted and the final official tabulation, and with blank and null votes kept separate. The sum matches the official result in each state and in Brazil, and the municipalities are the same as in the first round.",
"met.passo.3.tit": "Combine the two rounds",
"met.passo.3.txt": "The two rounds side by side, with the study's measures: Lula's share, change in share, vote gains, margin, share of the reversal, Lula's share of the combined gain and abstention. Each municipality is tagged with its region, state capital or rest of the state, and size. Everywhere, the votes the two gained equal the votes of the other first-round candidates, plus the change in turnout, minus the change in blank and null votes; the script checks that this equation balances to zero.",
"met.passo.4.tit": "Add up first-round votes by party",
"met.passo.4.txt": "The votes for senator and for federal, state and Federal District deputy, by municipality and party, from the TSE's open data. Each state's sum equals its official result in all 108 state–office pairs (27 states × 4 offices, counting governor, which comes in the same file), party by party.",
"met.passo.5.tit": "Place the parties on the scale",
"met.passo.5.txt": "Each party's position comes from the expert survey ({partidos}). With it, the script computes, by municipality and office, the % of votes for left-bloc parties (the right-bloc % is 100% minus this and the % for parties with no position), the continuous scale and the potential advantage, and checks the experts' averages against the published tables.",
"met.passo.6.tit": "Test the hypotheses and estimate with intervals",
"met.passo.6.txt": "The regressions of chapters 1, 3, 4 and 5, the 35 tests of the social data in chapter 8 (with IBGE data joined to the municipalities by IBGE code, before any cross-analysis), the ecological regression of where the votes came from (by place, with the TSE's polling-station data, assembled and checked beforehand), the funnel plot and the projection error, following the rules recorded before any calculation with the runoff by municipality ({incerteza}). Last, the five questions of the guided exploration (chapter 9), recorded before running them, but after seeing the results.",
"met.passo.7.tit": "Record the live count",
"met.passo.7.txt": "During the runoff count, a page read the TSE results, compared the count with the first round at the same proportion of registered voters counted, projected the final result and recorded each reading. The first-round voting machine reports, added up in the order they arrived, give the first-round count by % counted. The log and {como} are on the Live count page.",
"met.passo.7.como": "how the page worked",
"met.passo.8.tit": "From the datasets to the page",
"met.passo.8.txt": "The last step reads the files above and writes the page data, the state map (from the IBGE boundary files) and the files to download. It recomputes the shares and the changes from the vote counts, at full precision, and checks them against the datasets (note {n18}).",

// ---------- Sources (metodo.js) ----------
"met.fontes.intro": "Every address a piece of data came from, with the date and time it was downloaded and the check that was made. The study's numbers come from the TSE and, in chapter 8, from the IBGE (2022 Census and Municipal GDP, PIB dos Municípios 2023); the other sources give the parties' positions, the map outline or the context of a note.",
"met.fontes.tse": "Superior Electoral Court (TSE)",
"met.fontes.outras": "Other sources",
"met.fontes.contexto": "Context for the notes, without numbers",
